  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Snack-Size Chicken Option</h2>
<p>Most of DQ's chicken lives inside the <a href="/categories/chicken-strip-baskets">Chicken Strip Baskets</a>, which bundle strips with fries, Texas toast, and gravy. The 2-Piece Chicken Strips strip all of that away and give you just two strips and a dipping sauce. That makes it the lowest-cost entry point to DQ chicken and the right choice when you want protein without a full basket's ~1,000 calories.</p>
<h2>Why It Belongs in the 2-for-$5 Deal</h2>
<p>The 2-Piece Strips are one of the strongest picks in the <a href="/items/2-for-5-mix-match">2-for-$5 Mix &amp; Match</a>. Ordered on their own they are $3.49; paired with a second Mix &amp; Match item they effectively drop to $2.50. Pairing two orders of strips gives you four strips for $5.00 — noticeably cheaper per strip than the 4-Piece Basket if you do not need the fries and toast.</p>
<h2>Dipping Sauces</h2>
<p>Your strips come with one dipping sauce; extra sauces are usually about $0.30 each. Standard options include DQ Country Gravy, honey mustard, barbecue, ranch, and the signature sauces used on the strip baskets. If you like the FlameThrower or Honey BBQ basket flavors, you can request those sauces here at a fraction of the basket price.</p>
